      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T17:04:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Amit,\n\nSnapdragon boards do not support SVE. It is disabled in the firmware. For that reason, you should change the arch variant. We could add armv8.5-a or armv9-a+nosve if needed. Otherwise, we can downgrade to a supported variant.\n\nThanks,\n\nJake\n\nOn Thu, Mar 20, 2025, 11:54 AM Amit Pundir (Gerrit) \u003cnoreply-gerritcodereview+xsdllKGfcMULAk-DBHDTPw\u003d\u003d@\u003e wrote: google.com",
      "tag": "mailMessageId\u003d\u003cCAPqUeWmUQN9dRYxq8wpSSr9HyROnxMgrm08\u003dyKwsFprYbekHsg@mail.gmail.com\u003e",
      "revId": "7066039f37182e89820b8c0f4b075a2941336d15",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "633ca12f_75ad2d90",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1058860
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T17:04:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e el0_sve_acc+0x70/0x74\nI presume sm8x50 doesn\u0027t have either sve or sve2.  Clang assumes armv9 includes sve and sve2, per https://godbolt.org/z/zsTGEhEY7.\n\n\u003e \"target-features\"\u003d\"...+sve,+sve2...\"\n\nChanging the CPU is not going to fix this.  The fix will be to create a \"armv9-a_nosve\" arch variant and use `-march\u003darmv9-a+nosve2` for it.  @ccross@android.com - thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "5fa26259_b5e74844",
      "revId": "7066039f37182e89820b8c0f4b075a2941336d15",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77475267_7d0d92f7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1307979
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T18:41:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The immediate fix is to change `TARGET_ARCH_VARIANT` for this device to `armv8-2a-dotprod`. I\u0027ll upload this today.\n\nThe short-term fix would be to add `armv9-a-nosve` arch variant as pirama@ described.\n\nThe longer-term fix would be to add a new configuration variable `TARGET_ARCH_FEATURES` so that we wouldn\u0027t need to a new arch variant for every version and feature combination.",
      "parentUuid": "633ca12f_75ad2d90",
      "revId": "7066039f37182e89820b8c0f4b075a2941336d15",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
